research = heading('Research', 'Connecting observations, methods, and environmental questions.') + f'''
<div class="body-copy"><p>My research spans open land-use mapping, satellite time-series analysis, and the use of geospatial information to understand environmental risk.</p></div>
<section class="detail-section" id="land-use"><span class="tag">01 · LAND USE & OPEN DATA</span><h2>Combining satellite data with local knowledge</h2><p>Satellite imagery records the physical landscape. OpenStreetMap adds information about how people use it. My research explores how these sources can work together, including through machine learning, to produce detailed land-use information.</p><p>The OSMlanduse project applies this approach across Europe using Sentinel-2 observations and OpenStreetMap. My more recent work contributes land-use and land-cover mapping to <em>{PAABS_NAME}</em> (PAABS), funded through the International Climate Initiative (IKI) and implemented by GIZ with consortium partners.</p><div class="inline-links">{link('OSMlanduse','/projects/#osmlanduse')}{link('Paris Agreement & climate adaptation','/projects/#ukraine')}{link('Read the paper',PAPER,external=True)}</div></section>
<section class="detail-section" id="forest-change"><span class="tag">02 · FOREST CHANGE & CARBON</span><h2>Reading change through time</h2><p>Long satellite records make it possible to study how forests change. My doctoral work at Wageningen University investigated tropical deforestation monitoring using Landsat time series and breakpoint detection. A 2016 study compared eight vegetation indices across Brazil, Ethiopia and Vietnam.</p><p>This work connects forest monitoring with REDD+ and greenhouse-gas estimation. In Central Vietnam, satellite observations and forest inventories were combined to estimate carbon emissions and removals from land-cover change. Related applied work includes Xe Pian in Lao PDR and forest-change monitoring with WWF in the KAZA conservation area.</p><div class="inline-links">{link('Vegetation-index study',VEGETATION_STUDY,external=True)}{link('Carbon-emissions study',CARBON_STUDY,external=True)}{link('REDD+ chapter',REDD_CHAPTER,external=True)}{link('Doctoral thesis',THESIS,external=True)}{link('Past work','/projects/#past-work')}</div></section>
<section class="detail-section" id="risk"><span class="tag">03 · RISK & ADAPTATION</span><h2>Environmental information for decisions</h2><p>My work also addresses environmental hazards. {FRAME_NAME} (FRAME) makes flood scenarios and adaptation information explorable through web tools for Huế and Central Vietnam. It was developed within FloodAdaptVN, whose current implementation phase is funded by the German Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR). A separate collaborative study uses Sentinel-1 interferometry to examine ground deformation after the March 2025 earthquake in Mandalay, Myanmar.</p><div class="inline-links">{link('Explore FRAME',FRAME,external=True)}{link('Vietnam project overview','/projects/#frame')}{link('Mandalay study','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.srs.2025.100358',external=True)}</div></section>'''

projects = heading('Projects', 'From flood resilience in Vietnam to land monitoring in Ukraine: research, platforms, and open data you can explore.') + f'''
<nav class="project-index" aria-label="Jump to a project"><a href="#frame">Flood risk · Vietnam</a><a href="#ukraine">Paris Agreement · Ukraine</a><a href="#border-observatory">Trade & border monitoring</a><a href="#osmlanduse">OSM Land Use · Heidelberg</a><a href="#past-work">Past work</a></nav>
<section class="project" id="frame"><span class="tag">FLOOD RESILIENCE · HUẾ, VIETNAM</span><h2>{FRAME_NAME}</h2>{project_context("FRAME · FloodAdaptVN · BMFTR funding")}<p>How can flood-risk research become something people can explore and use? My work on FRAME connects geospatial data, flood scenarios, and accessible web tools for Huế and Central Vietnam.</p><p>The platform is part of FloodAdaptVN: <em>Integrating Ecosystem-based Approaches into Flood Risk Management for Adaptive and Sustainable Urban Development in Central Viet Nam</em>. The current implementation phase runs from June 2025 to May 2027 and is funded by the German Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR) through the Sustainable Development of Urban Regions (SURE) initiative.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Flood-risk platform · English',FRAME,external=True)}{link('Flood-risk platform · Tiếng Việt',FRAME_VN,external=True)}{link('FloodAdaptVN project',FLOODADAPT,external=True)}</div>
<div class="tool-grid">
<a href="{FRAME_APP}scenario-explorer/"><span class="tag">EXPLORE SCENARIOS</span><h3>How might risk change?</h3><p>Compare flood depths and urban-growth scenarios for 2030 and 2050.</p><span class="tool-action">Open scenario explorer {icon('external')}</span></a>
<a href="{FRAME_APP}flood-adaptation-products/"><span class="tag">EXPLORE ADAPTATION</span><h3>What can we do?</h3><p>Explore ecosystem-based adaptation, adaptation economics, water quality, and parking guidance.</p><span class="tool-action">Browse FRAME tools {icon('external')}</span></a>
</div><p class="project-meta">Planning and research tools based on historical observations and modelled scenarios.</p><div class="project-links">{link('How FRAME works','https://elib.dlr.de/217324/',external=True)}{link('Project updates','https://floodadapt.eoc.dlr.de/news/index.html',external=True)}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="ukraine"><span class="tag">LAND MONITORING · UKRAINE · 2025–PRESENT</span><h2>{PAABS_TITLE}</h2>{project_context("International Climate Initiative (IKI) · GIZ")}<p><em>{PAABS_NAME}</em> (PAABS) is funded through the International Climate Initiative (IKI) and implemented by Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) GmbH with consortium partners.</p><p>Since October 2025, I have contributed to the programme’s land-monitoring work in Ukraine. In 2026, I coordinated land-use and land-cover classification combining Sentinel-2 observations, OpenStreetMap-derived training data, and reproducible processing workflows.</p><p>My paabs.de research atlas makes this land-monitoring work accessible to project partners. The work supports Ukraine’s Land Parcel Identification System and land-use, land-use-change and forestry reporting. It connects detailed satellite mapping with the information needed for climate policy.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Land-monitoring portal',PAABS,external=True)}{link('Platform screenshot','/assets/paabs-platform.webp',external=True)}{link('Programme · GIZ',PAABS_PROGRAMME,external=True)}{link('Funding · IKI',PAABS_IKI,external=True)}{link('My contribution',LINKEDIN,external=True)}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="border-observatory"><span class="tag">EARTH OBSERVATION · AFRICA · RESEARCH PREVIEW</span><h2>{TRADE_TITLE}</h2>{project_context("World Bank · Border Observatory")}<p>Satellite-based monitoring of vehicle occupancy supports research on congestion, logistics and trade at African border crossings. Move from an Africa-wide overview to individual border crossings, then explore how estimated occupied area varies across the observation archive. This interactive viewer connects map features with historical satellite-derived summaries.</p><p class="project-meta">The indicator measures estimated occupied area; it does not directly measure vehicle counts, queues, or crossing times.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Open Border Observatory',WBEO,external=True)}{link('Explore Chirundu in 3D',CHIRUNDU,external=True)}{link('World Bank reproducibility package',WB_REPRODUCIBILITY,external=True)}{link('WBEO catalogue','https://wbearthobservation.org/catalogue/',external=True)}</div></section>
''' + f'''
<section class="project" id="osmlanduse"><span class="tag">LAND USE · HEIDELBERG COLLABORATION</span><h2>OSM Land Use</h2>{project_context("Heidelberg University · HeiGIT")}<p>Explore OpenStreetMap’s land-use and land-cover information through the interactive OSM Landuse Landcover platform. I co-led the project with Alexander Zipf, working with colleagues at Heidelberg University and HeiGIT.</p><p>My contribution includes the deep-learning methods for filling gaps in OpenStreetMap coverage using Sentinel-2 imagery, developed with Hao Li and Zhaoyan Wu. The website was developed by Michael Auer and Moritz Schott; the platform’s “Info &amp; Contact” section credits the wider team.</p><p>The associated 10-metre European land-use dataset combines OpenStreetMap and Sentinel-2, connecting volunteered geographic information with satellite observations and deep learning.</p><p class="project-meta">2020 reference year · Published in Scientific Data, 2025 · Joint first authors: Michael Schultz and Hao Li</p><div class="project-links">{link('Explore the map',OSMLANDUSE,external=True)}{link('Platform screenshot','/assets/osmlanduse-portal.webp',external=True)}{link('Get the data',DATA,external=True)}{link('Source code',REPO,external=True)}{link('Paper',PAPER,external=True)}</div><figure class="project-figure"><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04703-8/figures/2"><img src="/assets/osmlanduse-map.webp" width="1900" height="1345" alt="European land-use map and regional comparisons from the OSMlanduse study" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>{credit}</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="section" id="past-work"><h2>Past work & experience</h2><p class="body-copy" style="margin-top:16px">Earlier research and consulting on forest monitoring, REDD+ and greenhouse-gas estimation, with work in conservation landscapes and climate reporting.</p></section>
<section class="project" id="forest-carbon"><span class="tag">LUCCI · CENTRAL VIETNAM · 2011–2016</span><h2>Forest carbon & greenhouse-gas estimation</h2><p>Within LUCCI, my work connected satellite time series with forest-change mapping and carbon accounting. The 2016 Carbon Management study combined Landsat land-cover observations with forest inventories to estimate carbon emissions and removals in the Vu Gia Thu Bon basin, including biomass and soil carbon.</p><p>The 2017 chapter <em>Forest Change and REDD+ Strategies</em> connects forest monitoring and carbon assessment with local REDD+ planning.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Carbon study · 2016',CARBON_STUDY,external=True)}{link('REDD+ chapter · 2017',REDD_CHAPTER,external=True)}{link('Study figure','/assets/past-carbon-vietnam.webp',external=True)}{link('Bibliography record','/publications/#MS-DF2E7AF1')}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="xe-pian"><span class="tag">XE PIAN · LAO PDR · 2011–2020</span><h2>REDD+ monitoring for forest-carbon projects</h2><p>I contributed remote-sensing and time-series workflows to the Xe Pian REDD+ project in Lao PDR, working with Österreichische Bundesforste and WWF. My work included baseline modelling, land-use-change analysis, reporting, ground-reference validation, audit support and training for local staff.</p><p>The work supported project preparation and monitoring under the Verified Carbon Standard (VCS). It linked satellite-based activity data with the information needed to estimate forest-carbon emissions and establish a reference baseline.</p><div class="project-links">{link('WWF / Bundesforste project',XE_PIAN,external=True)}{link('WWF factsheet',XE_PIAN_FACTSHEET,external=True)}{link('Related REDD+ research',REDD_CHAPTER,external=True)}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="forest-monitoring"><span class="tag">LANDSAT METHODS · 2016 STUDIES · PHD 2018</span><h2>Tropical Forest Monitoring</h2>{project_context("PhD thesis · Wageningen University")}<p>Which satellite indices best reveal forest loss? My 2016 study compared eight Landsat vegetation indices with BFAST Monitor across tropical sites in Brazil, Ethiopia and Vietnam. It examined detection accuracy and the effects of vegetation signals, clouds and observation availability.</p><p>A companion 2016 study investigated error sources in BFAST Monitor. Both studies form part of my 2018 Wageningen doctoral thesis on tropical deforestation monitoring.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Vegetation-index paper',VEGETATION_STUDY,external=True)}{link('Error-sources paper','https://doi.org/10.1109/JSTARS.2015.2477473',external=True)}{link('Spider plots','/assets/past-vegetation-spider.webp',external=True)}{link('Bar plots','/assets/past-vegetation-indices.webp',external=True)}{link('Doctoral thesis',THESIS,external=True)}{link('Bibliography record','/publications/#MS-3B237F91')}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="wwf-kaza"><span class="tag">SOUTHERN AFRICA · 2016–2018</span><h2>Kavango–Zambezi Monitoring</h2>{project_context("WWF · Peace Parks Foundation")}<p>Working with WWF and Peace Parks Foundation, I developed Landsat-based land-cover and vegetation-change monitoring for the Kavango–Zambezi Transfrontier Conservation Area. The work connected field validation, operational processing workflows and staff training with conservation monitoring.</p><p>The associated 2018 paper examines forest-cover and vegetation degradation detection using BFAST Monitor. Field validation in Zambia and Namibia helped connect satellite-based change estimates with conditions on the ground.</p><div class="project-links">{link('WWF project',WWF_KAZA,external=True)}{link('Research paper · 2018',KAZA_STUDY,external=True)}{link('Study-area figure','/assets/past-wwf-kaza.webp',external=True)}{link('Bibliography record','/publications/#MS-0D2C2625')}</div></section>
<section class="project" id="greenhouse-gases"><span class="tag">HEIDELBERG · GREENHOUSE-GAS ESTIMATION</span><h2>Emissions across land use and transport</h2><p>My later work extended spatial greenhouse-gas estimation to land-use change and road transport. The 2023 studies address carbon fluxes in Baden-Württemberg and street-level private-vehicle emissions in Berlin using open data.</p><div class="project-links">{link('Land-use carbon fluxes',CARBON_FLUXES,external=True)}{link('Vehicle-emissions study',VEHICLE_EMISSIONS,external=True)}{link('Berlin emissions dataset','https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7557041',external=True)}</div></section>'''

